    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel`, keeping structural impact low by touching only small, low-complexity units:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`). This regenerates the `OwnerDto` with `get/setMembershipLevel(Integer)` and drops `membershipTier` from the response.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** (1 line, CC=1 abstract method, tiny `WMC_other`) \u2014 Changed the `@Mapping` expression to compute the level: `1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount==0 ? 1 : 0)`. Max is 3, so the cap is inherent.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (1 line) \u2014 The household-override that previously set the top tier `\"GOLD\"` now sets `setMembershipLevel(4)`, consistent with \"level 4 is reserved\" above the creation cap of 3.\n\nThe create audit line (`OwnerAuditListener`) never recorded the tier, so it needed no change. The new `AcceptanceTest` (owner with email + zero namesakes \u2192 level 3, capped) passes, and the full build compiles and succeeds.",
